[154.629061, "o", "root@08c0120c5b18:/app# "]
[154.703604, "i", "cat >> README.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Resume and crash recovery\n\nThe checkpoint is a commit record for a durable prefix of live documents. Its\n`last_id` is exclusive on the next source query (IDs need not be contiguous).\n`docs` counts that prefix, and `shards` records the committed byte length of each\nshard. Index rows and the checksum/minhash algorithms are unchanged.\n\nThe worker retains block buffering: it fsyncs all affected shards (including\nrotated files), syncs the index directory, then writes and fsyncs a temporary\ncheckpoint, atomically replaces the old checkpoint, and syncs its directory.\nSIGTERM/SIGINT/SIGHUP request a stop after the current document; the worker commits\nthat prefix and exits 75. No work or I/O is done in the signal handler.\n\nAfter an abrupt kill, the next invocation first truncates uncommitted shard tails\nand removes uncommitted shards using the last checkpoint. This rollback is itself\nrestartable, and runs even for an already-complete checkpoint. Missing committed\nbytes or corrupt versioned"]
[154.703888, "i", " checkpoints cause an error rather than silently\nskipping documents or discarding committed progress. Legacy checkpoints from the\nold worker have no reliable durable boundary, so they trigger a one-time rebuild.\nUse `./jobs reindex` to retain the supervisor's single-run lock; do not run workers\nconcurrently against the same output. `./jobs clean` deliberately discards all\nprogress and should only be used when no reindex is running.\n\nA completed checkpoint describes one reindex of a stable source corpus. To build\na new generation after source edits/deletions, explicitly clean and reindex.\nEOF\n"]
[154.723178, "o", "cat >> README.md <<'EOF'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[154.72352, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Resume and crash recovery\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> The checkpoint is a commit record for a durable prefix of live documents. Its\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> `last_id` is exclusive on the next source query (IDs need not be contiguous).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[154.72363, "o", "`docs` counts that prefix, and `shards` records the committed byte length of each\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> shard. Index rows and the checksum/minhash algorithms are unchanged.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[154.723706, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[154.723759, "o", "The worker retains block buffering: it fsyncs all affected shards (including\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[154.723808, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[154.723887, "o", "rotated files), syncs the index directory, then writes and fsyncs a temporary\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[154.723939, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[154.724011, "o", "checkpoint, atomically replaces the old checkpoint, and syncs its directory.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[154.724063, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[154.724137, "o", "SIGTERM/SIGINT/SIGHUP request a stop after the current document; the worker commits\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[154.724185, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[154.724266, "o", "that prefix and exits 75. No work or I/O is done in the signal handler.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[154.724313, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[154.724412, "o", "After an abrupt kill, the next invocation first truncates uncommitted shard tails\r\n"]
[154.72446, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[154.724542, "o", "and removes uncommitted shards using the last checkpoint. This rollback is itself\r\n"]
[154.724589, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[154.724674, "o", "restartable, and runs even for an already-complete checkpoint. Missing committed\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[154.724747, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[154.724885, "o", "bytes or corrupt versioned checkpoints cause an error rather than silently\r\n"]
[154.724903, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[154.72497, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[154.725029, "o", "skipping documents or discarding committed progress. Legacy checkpoints from the"]
[154.72557, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[154.72564, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[154.725693, "o", "> "]
[154.726046, "o", "old worker have no reliable durable boundary, so they trigger a one-time rebuild.\r\n"]
[154.726064, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[154.726151, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[154.72674, "o", "Use `./jobs reindex` to retain the supervisor's single-run lock; do not run workers\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[154.726813, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[154.726955, "o", "concurrently against the same output. `./jobs clean` deliberately discards all"]
[154.727311, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[154.727331, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[154.72757, "o", "progress and should only be used when no reindex is running.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[154.727588, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[154.727691, "o", "A completed checkpoint describes one reindex of a stable source corpus. To build"]
[154.728033, "o", "\r\n"]
[154.729865, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[154.729944, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[154.738562, "o", "a new generation after source edits/deletions, explicitly clean and reindex.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> EOF\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004hroot@08c0120c5b18:/app# "]
